### Task 4: The list is pushed again whenever it changes

**Files:**
- Modify: `hosted/infra/lib/handlers/ws.ts` (`$disconnect`, the `watch` message)
- Test: `hosted/infra/test/ws.test.ts`

**Interfaces:**
- Consumes: `tellDecks` from Task 3.
- Produces: no new exports.

- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**

```ts
it("tells a deck when a run is opened and when the page goes", async () => {
  const live = memoryLive();
  const posted: Array<[string, string]> = [];
  const poster: Poster = { post: async (id, data) => (posted.push([id, data]), "ok") };
  const deps = depsWith({ live, poster });
  await route({ requestContext: { routeKey: "$connect", connectionId: "deck1" }, queryStringParameters: { token: "good", as: "deck" } }, deps);
  await route({ requestContext: { routeKey: "$connect", connectionId: "page" }, queryStringParameters: { token: "good" } }, deps);
  posted.length = 0;

  await route({ requestContext: { routeKey: "$default", connectionId: "page" }, body: JSON.stringify({ t: "watch", id: "s1" }) }, deps);
  expect(JSON.parse(posted.at(-1)![1]).runs.map((r: { id: string }) => r.id)).toEqual(["s1"]);

  posted.length = 0;
  await route({ requestContext: { routeKey: "$disconnect", connectionId: "page" } }, deps);
  expect(JSON.parse(posted.at(-1)![1]).runs).toEqual([]);
});
```

- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**

Run: `npm test -w hosted/infra -- ws`
Expected: FAIL — nothing posted after the watch.

- [ ] **Step 3: Tell the decks on both edges**

In the `watch` message branch, after `await deps.live.watch(...)`:

```ts
await deps.live.watch(connectionId, m["id"], conn.sub, now());
// A run just came under a device. A deck that has been sitting on "No
// run open" all evening is the one thing waiting to hear it.
await tellDecks(conn.sub);
return { statusCode: 200 };
```

In `$disconnect`, after the existing `tellWhoIsAttached` call:

```ts
const leaving = await deps.live.connection(connectionId);
await deps.live.disconnect(connectionId);
if (leaving?.control && leaving.run) await tellWhoIsAttached(leaving.run);
// A page closing may have been the last thing holding a run, and a deck
// whose keys still look live is worse than one that says so.
if (leaving && !leaving.deck && writes(leaving)) await tellDecks(leaving.sub);
return { statusCode: 200 };
```

Note `heldRuns`/`tellDecks` must be hoisted above `$disconnect` too — define both immediately after `const now = ...` at the top of `route`.

- [ ] **Step 4: Run the tests**

Run: `npm test -w hosted/infra`
Expected: PASS.

- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**

```bash
npm run typecheck
git add hosted/infra/lib/handlers/ws.ts hosted/infra/test/ws.test.ts
git commit -m "feat(live): the held-run list is pushed when it changes"
```

